INFO:supervisor:Supervisor created execution plan (goal="Identify the top-3 single-month volume anomalies (region × product_line) in offline_data/regional_sales.csv by computing each month's volume relative to its own 24-month mean, report the multiples and corresponding return rates, assess whether each spike is genuine demand or channel stuffing, and produce a Markdown report with embedded charts saved to disk."):
1. Inspect CSV structure: Read offline_data/regional_sales.csv: list all column names, total row count, date range (min/max of the month column), unique regions, unique product lines, and print first 5 rows as sample → db_agent
2. Compute 24-month baseline & anomaly multiples: Using the CSV, for each (region × product_line) compute the 24-month rolling mean of monthly sales volume; then for every month compute the ratio = that month's volume / its own 24-month mean. Save the full result table to a CSV file (e.g. offline_data/anomaly_multiples.csv) with columns: region, product_line, month, monthly_volume, rolling_24m_mean, multiple → code_agent
3. Identify top-3 anomalies & fetch return rates: From the anomaly_multiples.csv, select the top 3 (region, product_line, month) rows by multiple. For each, look up the corresponding return_rate (or equivalent column) from the original regional_sales.csv. Save a small summary CSV (offline_data/top3_anomalies.csv) with columns: rank, region, product_line, month, monthly_volume, rolling_24m_mean, multiple, return_rate → code_agent
4. Assess demand vs channel-stuffing signals: For each of the top-3 anomalies, compute auxiliary signals from the CSV: (a) return_rate for that month vs the 24-month average return_rate for the same region×product_line; (b) whether the following 1–3 months show a volume drop (reversion); (c) whether the spike is isolated (single-month) or sustained. Save a signals CSV (offline_data/anomaly_signals.csv) → code_agent
5. Generate charts: Create 2–3 PNG charts: (1) bar chart of top-3 multiples; (2) line chart showing the 24-month volume trend for each top-3 combination with the anomaly month highlighted; (3) return-rate comparison bar chart. Save all PNGs to offline_data/charts/ → code_agent
6. Write Markdown report: Write a comprehensive Markdown report (offline_data/regional_sales_anomaly_report.md) with: H1 title, data table of top-3 anomalies, embedded PNG charts, every key number annotated with source in the format '（来源：offline_data/regional_sales.csv 的 <列名>，<聚合口径与样本行数>）' or '（来源：由前述两行计算）', and a concluding paragraph judging whether each spike is genuine demand or channel stuffing. All conclusions must derive solely from the local CSV → code_agent
